// A nested function is scoped to its containing function and does not leak
// (cx_syntax.md): `inner()` at the top level is "call to undefined function".
// It ran before — printing 99 twice — because nested functions kept their bare
// names and the interpreter registered them globally (known_issues §44).
fnc: outer() {
    fnc: inner() {
        print(99)
    }
    inner()
}
outer()
inner()
